yarn.lock

# CI steps that configure registry auth can drop a real credential into a
# working-tree .npmrc (this repo's runners get one pointing at
# npm.pkg.github.com, written after checkout). Nothing here is meant to be
# committed — ignore it so a stray `git add .` in a future change can't publish
# one. (Releases use OIDC trusted publishing and need no committed token.)
#
# NOT `actions/setup-node` with `registry-url:` — that writes
# $RUNNER_TEMP/.npmrc and points npm at it via NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG, outside
# the work tree where `git add` can't reach it. The only such step here is
# release.yml, tag-gated and pointed at registry.npmjs.org, which is a
# different registry from the file that actually appears.
.npmrc
